ass in Siem Reap or Phnom Penh — an under-sung Southeast-Asian table","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"venue/DMC 10-15%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","river":"destination","romance":"destination","senior":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC","venue"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Angkor + countryside by bike (marked routes)","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~$25-90/pp","timing":"year-round","draw_rank":1,"hook":"the temples and rice-paddy lanes by bicycle, plus Tonlé Sap boating — the active layer. 🚩 UXO: established/marked routes only","si":"adventure","blurb":"the temples and rice-paddy lanes by bicycle, plus Tonlé Sap boating — the active layer. 🚩 UXO: established/marked routes only","when":"year-round","commission":"operator/affiliate 10-15%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","culture"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","culinary":"destination","culture":"evidenced","deepdive":"destination","river":"destination","romance":"destination","senior":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["operator","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Angkor sunrise + a small-ship suite","si_tag":"romance","status":"future","tier":"premier","price_band":"~$3,000-7,000+/pp","timing":"dry Nov-Apr ideal","draw_rank":1,"hook":"sunrise over Angkor Wat''s reflecting pools, then a 5-star small-ship suite up the Tonlé Sap — a quiet, extraordinary honeymoon arc","si":"romance","blurb":"sunrise over Angkor Wat''s reflecting pools, then a 5-star small-ship suite up the Tonlé Sap — a quiet, extraordinary honeymoon arc","when":"dry Nov-Apr ideal","commission":"cruise-line/host 10-16%","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","deepdive":"destination","river":"destination","romance":"primary","senior":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":16,"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band"},{"name":"The low-exertion river cruise + Angkor","si_tag":"senior","status":"future","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~$2,500-5,000/pp","timing":"dry Nov-Apr ideal","draw_rank":1,"hook":"an all-in small-ship cruise with step-managed temple touring — a rich, low-mobility itinerary, flights linking Siem Reap","si":"senior","blurb":"an all-in small-ship cruise with step-managed temple touring — a rich, low-mobility itinerary, flights linking Siem Reap","when":"dry Nov-Apr ideal","commission":"cruise-line/DMC 10-16%","wells":["move","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture","river","senior"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"destination","culture":"evidenced","deepdive":"destination","river":"evidenced","romance":"destination","senior":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":16,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cambodia?","a":"Landmines/UXO - the safety-spine item, avalanche-level weight. Contamination persists in provinces including Siem Reap; stay strictly on marked paths and cleared temple routes, never wander into fields or unmarked ground. Petty bag-snatch is the secondary caution.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cambodia","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the closed Thai borders a problem for a Mekong cruise?","a":"No. All Cambodia-Thailand land crossings are closed (2026), but the Mekong cruise enters Cambodia by river from Vietnam at Tan Chau, and Siem Reap/Phnom Penh connect by flight - so cruise itineraries are unaffected. It only matters for overland Thailand-Cambodia travel.","source":"kh.usembassy.gov","si_tag":"river"},{"q":"When is the best time to cruise the Cambodian Mekong?","a":"Roughly November-April (dry, cooler); the Tonle Sap is highest and most navigable after the wet season (Oct-Dec), when the lake and its floating villages are fullest.","source":"uniworld.com","si_tag":"river"},{"q":"Which lines cruise the Cambodian Mekong?","a":"Confirmed: Aqua Expeditions (Aqua Mekong), Pandaw, Scenic, Uniworld, CroisiEurope and Viking - most on Vietnam-Cambodia itineraries, Siem Reap to Phnom Penh via the Tonle Sap and Kampong Cham.","source":"adventure-life.com","si_tag":"river"},{"q":"Is Angkor Wat worth building the trip around?","a":"Yes - Angkor is the largest religious monument on earth and the reason most cruises terminate at Siem Reap; pair the temples with the Tonle Sap floating villages and a Phnom Penh Khmer-Rouge history day for the full Cambodian arc.","source":"adventure-life.com","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cambodia Mekong Travel Guide: River Cruises, Angkor Wat & the Tonle Sap","meta_description":"Plan Cambodia''s Mekong - Phnom Penh to Siem Reap river cruises (Aqua Expeditions, Pandaw, Scenic, Uniworld), Angkor Wat, the Tonle Sap floating villages and the Khmer-Rouge history sites, with the real safety picture.","slug":"mekong-cambodia","primary_keyword":"Cambodia Mekong travel guide","long_tail":["Cambodia Mekong river cruise Phnom Penh Siem Reap 2026","Angkor Wat sunrise","Tonle Sap floating villages","is Cambodia safe to visit 2026","Cambodia landmine safety","Aqua Mekong Cambodia"],"search_language":"km-KH","local_keywords":["Mekong Kampuchea","Angkor Wat","Tonle Sap","Phnom Penh","Siem Reap"],"hreflang":["en","km-KH"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-29","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","nam